00:05:37.178 --> 00:05:39.207
Give us a Charles description.

00:05:39.207 --> 00:05:41.439
(Charles laughing)

00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:43.004
Of what this experience is like.

00:05:43.004 --> 00:05:45.862
- It just taste like having a
great time with good people.

00:05:45.862 --> 00:05:49.414
- Having a great time
with good people, yeah?

00:05:49.414 --> 00:05:51.001
No, no, wait with me.

00:05:51.001 --> 00:05:55.881
You gotta wait your turn.
(Charles laughing)

00:05:55.881 --> 00:05:56.909
Nice, right?

00:05:56.909 --> 00:05:58.087
- Right, right.

00:05:58.087 --> 00:05:59.331
Now scoop.

00:05:59.331 --> 00:06:01.073
- Over your side, yeah.

00:06:01.073 --> 00:06:02.240
But you don't.

00:06:03.574 --> 00:06:04.633
Scoop on your side!

00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:07.402
- Yeah, but I haven't done
anything to that, have I?

00:06:07.402 --> 00:06:10.277
- Joe, have you got any
more curry facts there?

00:06:10.277 --> 00:06:12.922
- No, I've got curry jokes.

00:06:12.922 --> 00:06:15.357
My grandad had an accident eating curry.

00:06:15.357 --> 00:06:17.103
Yeah, he slipped into a coma.

00:06:17.103 --> 00:06:18.789
(Charles laughing)

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:21.439
But it's fine, for all he wanted,

00:06:21.439 --> 00:06:23.689
he ended up next to my nan.

00:06:24.686 --> 00:06:25.754
That's two jokes.

00:06:25.754 --> 00:06:27.469
- God, that is--
- Two jokes.

00:06:27.469 --> 00:06:30.469
(gravelly laughing)

00:06:32.118 --> 00:06:33.722
(comical wheezing)

00:06:33.722 --> 00:06:34.609
- Right, that's enough of that.

00:06:34.609 --> 00:06:37.753
Our final stop is in Mayfair.

00:06:37.753 --> 00:06:38.731
- Swanky.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.870
- Also, they need a week's prep time

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:42.453
to make this masterpiece.

00:06:42.453 --> 00:06:45.536
(gentle piano music)

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.968
- We are at Benares restaurant,
and my name is Atul Kochhar,

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.791
and I'm chef patron of this restaurant.

00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:58.068
We won our Michelin Star in 2007,

00:06:58.068 --> 00:07:00.052
and it's almost 10 years
we have maintained it.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.084
Benares menu is always
about what's happening

00:07:02.084 --> 00:07:04.207
at the moment in this particular month.

00:07:04.207 --> 00:07:07.301
I strongly believe our ethos
are, if we let mother nature

00:07:07.301 --> 00:07:08.949
do the job really well, as a cook,

00:07:08.949 --> 00:07:10.647
I would have to do very little.

00:07:10.647 --> 00:07:12.097
Today, you'll be tasting truffle

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:14.221
and mushroom and saffron kulcha.

00:07:14.221 --> 00:07:16.675
Kulcha is a stuffed naan, so to speak,

00:07:16.675 --> 00:07:19.208
which will be smothered
with gold leaf butter.

00:07:19.208 --> 00:07:22.020
And then, it's drizzled with
Single Estate Balsamic Vinegar,

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.063
which is really, really fantastic.

00:07:24.063 --> 00:07:26.550
And this will be served
with venison keema,

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.140
starting with a garam masala.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.707
When we say garam masala, it's
cinnamon, cardamom, clove,

00:07:30.707 --> 00:07:33.977
and then add salt, onion,
and garlic, put the meat in.

00:07:33.977 --> 00:07:36.732
And then, when we finish it
with a little bit of tomato,

00:07:36.732 --> 00:07:38.955
at that time, just to thicken the keema,

00:07:38.955 --> 00:07:40.866
really, handful of chocolate.

00:07:40.866 --> 00:07:42.741
That chocolate actually makes the sauce,

00:07:42.741 --> 00:07:45.185
and morel mushrooms, which
are really at the peak

00:07:45.185 --> 00:07:47.907
at the moment, so flavors will
be humongous and really big.

00:07:47.907 --> 00:07:51.047
And that is the most
exclusive dish on our menu.

00:07:51.047 --> 00:07:53.371
We sell it for 210 pounds.

00:07:53.371 --> 00:07:54.234
- I'm ready.

00:07:54.234 --> 00:07:56.329
- You ready?
- I'm ready, formally.

00:07:56.329 --> 00:07:57.226
- So am I.

00:07:57.226 --> 00:08:00.559
- This is an incredibly exciting moment.

00:08:01.403 --> 00:08:03.388
- I am so pumped.

00:08:03.388 --> 00:08:05.815
Wealth just emanating from this dish.

00:08:05.815 --> 00:08:07.860
It really is something else to look at.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.775
- Jordan has obviously
dressed for the occasion.

00:08:10.775 --> 00:08:12.509
- [Jordan] I'm wearing shorts.

00:08:12.509 --> 00:08:14.401
- I was gonna say we should tear,

00:08:14.401 --> 00:08:17.089
but they've provided us with a weapon.

00:08:17.089 --> 00:08:20.601
Cut this into four pieces
so we can have two each.

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:21.780
- [Charles] There ya go, buddy.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.946
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:08:22.946 --> 00:08:26.196
(dramatic piano music)

00:08:32.698 --> 00:08:34.433
It's just really (bleeping) good.

00:08:34.433 --> 00:08:35.886
It's like a parade.

00:08:35.886 --> 00:08:37.894
There's just all this fancy-ass food

00:08:37.894 --> 00:08:39.423
going on tour through your mouth.

00:08:39.423 --> 00:08:40.812
They're chuckin' out venison,

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:42.329
they're chuckin' out bits gorals.

00:08:42.329 --> 00:08:44.023
They're like, hooray, hooray!

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.057
- Still like a curry with naan bread,

00:08:46.057 --> 00:08:50.936
it's just a really, really
special curry and naan bread.

00:08:50.936 --> 00:08:52.244
Can you taste the gold?

00:08:52.244 --> 00:08:53.869
- I can taste the gold.

00:08:53.869 --> 00:08:56.425
- That truly is the definition
of wealthy, isn't it?

00:08:56.425 --> 00:08:58.234
If you excrete gold?

00:08:58.234 --> 00:08:59.458
(enthused laughing)

00:08:59.458 --> 00:09:00.918
This is quite an experience.

00:09:00.918 --> 00:09:01.979
It's the setting--

00:09:01.979 --> 00:09:04.735
- Oh, oh, one thing
that I want to mention;

00:09:04.735 --> 00:09:06.475
the cutlery is magnetic.

00:09:06.475 --> 00:09:08.112
Hold on, wait, how we get this?

00:09:08.112 --> 00:09:09.414
See that? Wait.

00:09:09.414 --> 00:09:11.554
Pulls together.
(knives clanking)

00:09:11.554 --> 00:09:13.086
- You taste the venison, and then there's

00:09:13.086 --> 00:09:15.746
this very slight, bittery-sweetness

00:09:15.746 --> 00:09:17.206
that must come from the chocolate.

00:09:17.206 --> 00:09:19.370
- Which you're not really
used to in curries, really.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.538
Just this incredible fusion.

00:09:21.538 --> 00:09:24.585
- At the end of the day,
any food that is nice bread

00:09:24.585 --> 00:09:26.886
and something to dip it in or eat it with,

00:09:26.886 --> 00:09:28.349
I don't think you can go wrong.

00:09:28.349 --> 00:09:29.182
- [Charles] Yeah.

00:09:29.182 --> 00:09:31.283
- Wait, you've got to do the sound.

00:09:31.283 --> 00:09:33.456
Where did he get that from?

00:09:33.456 --> 00:09:34.862
- They let me have a fork.

00:09:34.862 --> 00:09:38.529
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:09:48.876 --> 00:09:49.878
- Worth It Winner time.

00:09:49.878 --> 00:09:52.450
So obviously, all the
restaurants were incredible.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.028
But, we have to decide
which was the most worth it.

00:09:55.028 --> 00:09:57.727
- My Worth It Winner has to be Benares.

00:09:57.727 --> 00:09:59.326
It was a curry with literal gold in it,

00:09:59.326 --> 00:10:00.667
why wouldn't it be the Worth It Winner?

00:10:00.667 --> 00:10:03.749
- I did like Benares a lot,
I did like Nazrul a lot,

00:10:03.749 --> 00:10:05.721
but my favorite is Karuna.

00:10:05.721 --> 00:10:07.039
I loved it, the street mart.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.863
I just felt very cool getting
food from a street market.

00:10:08.863 --> 00:10:09.811
- Yeah, it felt a bit hip.

00:10:09.811 --> 00:10:10.651
- Joe, what was yours?

00:10:10.651 --> 00:10:12.098
- Nazrul. Nazrul.

00:10:12.098 --> 00:10:14.318
The little tomato on the top, the crown.

00:10:14.318 --> 00:10:15.659
King of the curry.

00:10:15.659 --> 00:10:16.801
It was mwah.

00:10:16.801 --> 00:10:18.504
- It was what?

00:10:18.504 --> 00:10:20.487
- Mwah. It was like, mwah.

00:10:20.487 --> 00:10:21.826
- You mean, (kissing).

00:10:21.826 --> 00:10:22.659
- [Joe] Mwah.

00:10:22.659 --> 00:10:23.780
(kissing)

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.122
- Ooh, don't blow after.

00:10:25.122 --> 00:10:26.239
What are you blowing?

00:10:26.239 --> 00:10:28.866
I think we got through first episode.

00:10:28.866 --> 00:10:29.699
- [Charles] I think we've done it.

00:10:29.699 --> 00:10:30.532
- [Rich] I think we did it.

00:10:30.532 --> 00:10:31.365
- [Charles] Nice one, Lance.

00:10:31.365 --> 00:10:32.624
- Hope that was alright.

